fcitx5-slm-ime (2.2.0~SNAPSHOT-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * A choice of the user is not put where the model writes the ending of the
    word before in kana: a choice learned for いるの (要るの) made
    作っているのかな into 作って要るのかな.
  * A commit taken back with Ctrl+Shift+Insert, or erased with BackSpace right
    after it, is not learned.
  * When the user takes another text where an earlier choice was put in, that
    choice is forgotten however often it was made.
  * The model never runs on the fcitx5 main thread: a key that needs it waits
    for it on another thread, and the keys typed meanwhile wait behind it.
  * The weights are read on big-endian machines as well.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (2.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The candidate list opens once the model's candidates are in it, and its
    order does not change after that. It was shown in the dictionary's order
    and reordered without being shown again, so Space and the number keys
    chose another word than the one on the screen.
  * Page_Down and Page_Up turn the pages of the candidate list; the pages show
    the numbers 1 to 9, and a number key chooses on the page shown.
  * F5 shows the candidates of one kanji for the reading of the bunsetsu; F5
    again or Escape goes back to all the candidates.
  * Dictionary candidates that keep a small kana cut off from its syllable
    (気死ゃ for きしゃ) are no longer offered.
  * Digits and punctuation typed twice stay as they are in the reading: 400 was
    put in as 4っ0. Only a doubled consonant letter is a small tsu.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 07:08:08 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (2.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A letter typed during a conversion commits the conversion and starts the
    next reading. It was given back to the application, which put it before
    the conversion.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 03:01:10 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The conversion runs inside the engine, in C++ (Eigen) on the CPU: no
    conversion server, no Java and no PyTorch. The slm-ime-server package is
    removed on the upgrade; the history of the user's choices stays.
  * The model is retrained on readings cleaned with KANJIDIC2, JMdict and
    Sudachi, and with the readings in hiragana as the user types them.
  * Key bindings: a key binding profile (Default, MS-IME, ATOK) and the keys of
    every operation, in fcitx5-configtool, with Japanese labels.
  * F6 to F10 put the active phrasal unit in hiragana, katakana, half-width
    katakana, full-width letters and letters.
  * Nothing is learned in password and sensitive fields; the history is
    readable by the user only; a damaged model file is refused.
  * Anthy is found as anthy or anthy-unicode.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The model is trained on FineWeb-2 (Japanese web pages) besides the Japanese
    Wikipedia: the character error rate on web text falls from 7.25 % to 4.89 %.
  * The candidates from Anthy are put in order by the model, after the text before
    the phrasal unit, and are fetched in the background.
  * The last characters of a long conversion are no longer cut off.
  * Without the text before the cursor from the application, the engine sends the
    text committed before; Ctrl+Shift+Insert takes the last commit back.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0900

